      "writtenOn": "2019-05-03T03:08:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e IIUC, any choice for G !\u003d 1 is safe as long as P safe, so we don\u0027t have to check G\n\nShould we at least do some basic sanity checks on G? I might have missed it, but what stops the server from setting G\u003d1, or G\u003d0, or G\u003dP, or silly values like G\u003eP?",
      "parentUuid": "26dabba4_a36719ef",
      "revId": "1e7b6908c39e0c2b537de14c038bcf029a1f4575",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "febdb147_1703ac19",
        "filename": "ssh/kex.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 597,
      "author": {
        "id": 11715
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-03T16:48:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "DH with negotiated parameters is one of those things we kind of agreed never to do again, because literally everyone got it wrong at least once (https://cryptopals.com/sets/5) so let\u0027s check everything we can without breaking honest servers.\n\nSo yeah, prime(p), prime((p-1)/2), and g, K, and f all in the (1, p-1) range (1 and p-1 not included).",
      "parentUuid": "545656b4_1d610f19",
      "revId": "1e7b6908c39e0c2b537de14c038bcf029a1f4575",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c0d50583_5292fc72",
        "filename": "ssh/kex.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 597,
      "author": {
        "id": 16630
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-04T06:21:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I added the checks for g and K. But I do not understand what f is.",
      "parentUuid": "febdb147_1703ac19",
      "revId": "1e7b6908c39e0c2b537de14c038bcf029a1f4575",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c46eaa7e_6d487d24",
        "filename": "ssh/kex.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 766,
      "author": {
        "id": 5893
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-02T10:23:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you want to use group-exchange b/c security considerations (ie. you\u0027re worried that the NSA has a solved discrete log for some primes), you shouldn\u0027t hard code any prime at all.\n\nSince we\u0027re doing this so modern clients (us) can connect to backward servers, adding moduli has no real application for us.\n\nI propose hardcoding a single 2048 bit modulus, preferably the one from group14 (that\u0027s 2048 bit, right?), and documenting that the group exchange kex is not recommended server side. (we can always reconsider when we get requests for this).",
      "revId": "1e7b6908c39e0c2b537de14c038bcf029a1f4575",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "87a20c82_c3439a3c",
        "filename": "ssh/kex.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 766,
      "author": {
        "id": 16630
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-02T18:13:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am completely fine with implementing this key exchange only for the client, because I agree, that the use case to add this in the first place is to be able to talk to legacy servers. We could even go so far that we have a panic-ing Server implementation and a minimal server implementation (with only one hard coded moduli) in _test.go for tests only.\n\nExample:\n\nvar gexServerFunc func(gex *dhGEXSHA, p packetConn, rand io.Reader, magics *handshakeMagics, s Signer) (*kexResult, error)\n\nfunc (gex *dhGEXSHA) Server(p packetConn, rand io.Reader, magics *handshakeMagics, s Signer) (*kexResult, error) {\n\tif gexServerFunc !\u003d nil {\n\t\treturn gexServerFunc(gex, p, rand, magics, s)\n\t}\n\tpanic(\"server is not implemented for diffie-hellman-group-exchange-sha1 and diffie-hellman-group-exchange-sha256\")\n}",
      "parentUuid": "c46eaa7e_6d487d24",
      "revId": "1e7b6908c39e0c2b537de14c038bcf029a1f4575",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "32085886_66f10ae8",
        "filename": "ssh/kex.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 766,
      "author": {
        "id": 5893
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-02T18:30:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We must have the server half too, otherwise we can\u0027t test the client side. So, no panicking.",
      "parentUuid": "87a20c82_c3439a3c",
      "revId": "1e7b6908c39e0c2b537de14c038bcf029a1f4575",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7f540636_9ec54233",
        "filename": "ssh/kex.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 766,
      "author": {
        "id": 16630
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-02T19:00:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I am aware, that we need the server half during test. So for the test the gexServerFunc would be set to the server implementation (in init() func in _test.go) and therefore it does not panic in test but only when used in a real application.",
      "parentUuid": "32085886_66f10ae8",
      "revId": "1e7b6908c39e0c2b537de14c038bcf029a1f4575",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": true
    },
